{
  "id": "cb12",
  "title": "Tables",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "cb12-l1",
      "title": "OCCURS",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A table is a field that OCCURS several times: 05 MONTH-SALES PIC 9(5) OCCURS 6 TIMES. Each one is reached with a subscript in brackets: MONTH-SALES(1) to MONTH-SALES(6).",
        "OCCURS can't be used on an 01 level, so the table lives inside a group. A loop with VARYING walks through all the elements.",
        "A subscript outside the table, like MONTH-SALES(7), stops the job with IGZ0006S: subscript out of range."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. TABLE.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 SALES-TABLE.",
          "          05 MONTH-SALES PIC 9(5) OCCURS 6 TIMES.",
          "       01 M         PIC 9.",
          "       01 TOTAL     PIC 9(6) VALUE ZERO.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           MOVE 1200 TO MONTH-SALES(1).",
          "           MOVE 950  TO MONTH-SALES(2).",
          "           MOVE 1810 TO MONTH-SALES(3).",
          "           MOVE 700  TO MONTH-SALES(4).",
          "           MOVE 1305 TO MONTH-SALES(5).",
          "           MOVE 2045 TO MONTH-SALES(6).",
          "           PERFORM VARYING M FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL M > 6",
          "               ADD MONTH-SALES(M) TO TOTAL",
          "           END-PERFORM.",
          "           DISPLAY \"HALF YEAR: \" TOTAL.",
          "           DISPLAY \"MARCH:     \" MONTH-SALES(3).",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "HALF YEAR: 008010",
          "MARCH:     01810"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
