    {
      "id": "cb12-l2",
      "title": "Searching a Table",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Tables of fixed data, like month names or prices, are often filled with a trick: a group of FILLERs with VALUEs, and a second group that REDEFINES the same memory as a table.",
        "INDEXED BY gives the table an index, a counter made for it. SET MX TO 1 starts at the first element, and SEARCH goes through the table until a WHEN is true. AT END runs if nothing matched.",
        "SEARCH saves writing the loop yourself, and it reads like a sentence."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. LOOKUP.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 PRICE-DATA.",
          "          05 FILLER PIC X(9) VALUE \"COFFEE250\".",
          "          05 FILLER PIC X(9) VALUE \"TEA   180\".",
          "          05 FILLER PIC X(9) VALUE \"CAKE  320\".",
          "       01 PRICE-TABLE REDEFINES PRICE-DATA.",
          "          05 ITEM OCCURS 3 TIMES INDEXED BY PX.",
          "             10 ITEM-NAME  PIC X(6).",
          "             10 ITEM-PRICE PIC 9V99.",
          "       01 WANTED      PIC X(6).",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           ACCEPT WANTED.",
          "           SET PX TO 1.",
          "           SEARCH ITEM",
          "               AT END DISPLAY WANTED \"IS NOT ON THE MENU\"",
          "               WHEN ITEM-NAME(PX) = WANTED",
          "                   DISPLAY WANTED \"COSTS \" ITEM-PRICE(PX)",
          "           END-SEARCH.",
          "           ACCEPT WANTED.",
          "           SET PX TO 1.",
          "           SEARCH ITEM",
          "               AT END DISPLAY WANTED \"IS NOT ON THE MENU\"",
          "               WHEN ITEM-NAME(PX) = WANTED",
          "                   DISPLAY WANTED \"COSTS \" ITEM-PRICE(PX)",
          "           END-SEARCH.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "TEA   COSTS 180",
          "PIE   IS NOT ON THE MENU"
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "TEA",
          "PIE"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb12-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does REDEFINES do?",
          "options": [
            "Gives the same memory a second description",
            "Copies a field",
            "Deletes the old field",
            "Renames a field"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The FILLERs and the table are two views of the same bytes."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb12-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does SEARCH do when no WHEN is true for any element?",
          "options": [
            "Runs AT END",
            "Abends",
            "Runs the last WHEN",
            "Nothing at all"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "AT END is the \"not found\" case."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb12-l2-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Start the search at the first element.",
          "code": [
            "           ___ PX TO 1."
          ],
          "options": [
            "SET",
            "MOVE",
            "ADD",
            "INITIALIZE"
          ],
          "answer": "SET",
          "explanation": "Indexes are set with SET."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb12-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does INDEXED BY PX create?",
          "options": [
            "An index PX for walking through the table",
            "A sorted copy",
            "A key field",
            "A second table"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "SEARCH moves PX forward by itself."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb12-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why fill a table with FILLER VALUEs and REDEFINES?",
          "options": [
            "OCCURS items can't each get their own VALUE easily, so the values are written as a list first",
            "It's faster",
            "REDEFINES sorts them",
            "There's no other way to use OCCURS"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A classic COBOL trick for fixed tables."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb12-l2-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In the example, why is SET PX TO 1 written before the second SEARCH again?",
          "options": [
            "SEARCH starts where the index is, and the first search moved it",
            "SEARCH needs it twice",
            "To reset the table",
            "It isn't needed"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Forget it, and the second search starts in the middle."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cb12-l3",
      "title": "Text: STRING and INSPECT",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "COBOL fields have fixed sizes, so joining text needs STRING: STRING FIRST-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE \" \" LAST-NAME DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO FULL-NAME. DELIMITED BY SPACE stops at the first space; BY SIZE takes the whole field.",
        "INSPECT looks at the characters of a field: INSPECT TEXT TALLYING COUNTER FOR ALL \"E\" counts the E's, and INSPECT TEXT REPLACING ALL \"-\" BY \"/\" swaps characters.",
        "Note: TALLYING adds to the counter, so set it to zero first."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. TEXT.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 FIRST-NAME  PIC X(10) VALUE \"GRACE\".",
          "       01 LAST-NAME   PIC X(10) VALUE \"HOPPER\".",
          "       01 FULL-NAME   PIC X(21) VALUE SPACES.",
          "       01 DATE-TEXT   PIC X(10) VALUE \"1906-12-09\".",
          "       01 COUNTER     PIC 99 VALUE ZERO.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           STRING FIRST-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE \" \" DELIMITED BY SIZE",
          "               LAST-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE INTO FULL-NAME",
          "           END-STRING.",
          "           DISPLAY \"[\" FULL-NAME \"]\".",
          "           INSPECT FULL-NAME TALLYING COUNTER FOR ALL \"R\".",
          "           DISPLAY \"R COUNT: \" COUNTER.",
          "           INSPECT DATE-TEXT REPLACING ALL \"-\" BY \"/\".",
          "           DISPLAY \"BORN: \" DATE-TEXT.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "[GRACE HOPPER         ]",
          "R COUNT: 02",
          "BORN: 1906/12/09"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb12-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does DELIMITED BY SPACE do in STRING?",
          "options": [
            "Takes the field only up to its first space",
            "Adds a space",
            "Removes all spaces",
            "Takes the whole field"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "So the trailing spaces of a name aren't copied."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb12-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this job show?",
